cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use CreditICL, cite this software and record the exact Git commit used.
  Cite the underlying models and methodological papers separately.
type: software
title: "CreditICL: Credit-targeted synthetic priors for tabular foundation models"
authors:
  - family-names: Goethals
    given-names: Andreas
    affiliation: KU Leuven
    email: andreas.goethals@kuleuven.be
repository-code: https://github.com/andreasgoethals/CreditICL
url: https://github.com/andreasgoethals/CreditICL
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Research software for controlled synthetic-prior pretraining, continued
  pretraining and constrained adaptation of tabular foundation models for
  credit-risk benchmarks, with credit and out-of-domain evaluation. The MIT
  licence covers original project code; third-party code, data and model weights
  retain their own terms.
keywords:
  - tabular foundation models
  - credit risk
  - synthetic priors
  - continued pretraining
  - out-of-domain retention
